    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d111">

                <pb facs="0111" n="99" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg99"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">884.24/112</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Under Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Welles</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to President Roosevelt
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-06-18">June 18, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. President</hi>: Attached hereto for your
                    signature, if you approve, is a proposed reply to three communications which
                    have been received from the Emperor of Ethiopia.</p>
                <p>The only point calling for particular attention in our suggested reply is the
                    statement that this Government would welcome a diplomatic representative of
                    Ethiopia, the Emperor having indicated in one of his letters that he is anxious
                    to make such an appointment. As our Minister Resident, Mr. John K. Caldwell, is
                    shortly to proceed to Addis Ababa to open a legation there it is presumed that
                    we would be willing to have an Ethiopian diplomatic representative in
                    Washington.</p>
                <p>Faithfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sumner Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d111-a1.xml" xpointer="d111-a1"/>
            </div>
